    family-names: Takesue
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8585-5494"
    affiliation: >-
      Division of Transcriptomics, Medical Institute of Bioregulation,
      Kyushu University
repository-code: https://github.com/takeisue1270/Plasmid_Assembly_Designer
url: https://github.com/takeisue1270/Plasmid_Assembly_Designer
abstract: >-
  A documented procedure and two command-line tools for designing Golden Gate
  and HiFi assembly constructs from SnapGene .dna maps. The design is derived
  from the bases in the maps, the product map is built by splicing the backbone
  .dna, and the product is re-read from disk and verified before any oligo is
  ordered. The procedure also keeps the oligo list and the project record in
  step. Workbook and sheet names are configuration, not code.
keywords:
  - molecular cloning
  - Golden Gate assembly
  - HiFi assembly
  - SnapGene
  - plasmid map
  - sgRNA cloning
  - primer design
